  "method": "reviewed reading of the published interface: the CLI is closed source and no typed schema, SDK or vendor test of the stream-json output is published. The headless-mode documentation (html sha256 above) states the events, the step_update, tool_info, subagent_info and result members, the status values and the scope of the result counters; the public repository holds only README, CHANGELOG and examples, and its CHANGELOG at the pinned tag dates the format (stream-json, tool_info and subagent_info in 1.1.8, denied_actions in 1.1.27). The documentation calls its step_type list observed values, not a closed vocabulary, so the families below are documented plus observed on the 1.4.6 recordings; members only observed say so in their symbol. The CHANGELOG (1.1.8) calls step_type a stable, closed vocabulary, but its members are not published. Completeness is not established: a family not declared here may exist."
